.TH TEST-ONHOSTS 1 "October 2026" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Test-OnHosts \- run every test under tests/ on each host named
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Test-OnHosts
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.IR host ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Test-OnHosts
runs every test under
.I tests/
on each host named, in turn, and fails when any host's tests fail, naming each.
A name that is this machine's, by its short host name or localhost, runs here, through
.BR Test-Here (1).
Any other host gets a copy of this working tree's
.IR Home ,
.I bin
and
.IR tests ,
what git tracks and what is new and not ignored, in a folder of its own under
.IR ~/.local/state/noblefactor-engprod-tests ,
and runs its tests there over ssh: through
.B Test-Here
on macOS and Linux, and
.B Test-Here.ps1
on Windows, which is asked of the host.
The folder goes when its tests pass, and stays, named, when they fail.
.B make test HOSTS=\(dq\fIhost\fR ...\(dq
runs it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this manual page and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every host's tests passed.
.TP
.B 1
A host's tests failed; each is named.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error \- no host named.
.TP
.B 72
Critical file missing \- \fBDeclare-BashScript\fR is not in the repository's \fIHome/common/.local/bin\fR, or the repository's root cannot be entered.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bin/Test-OnHosts danoble-mbp-a danoble-ud24-1 danoble-wd11-3
make test HOSTS=\(dqdanoble-mbp-a danoble-ud24-1\(dq
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Test-Here (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR make (1)
